    "fullSolution": "**Find root of $f(x) = x^3 - 2$ using Newton's method, $x_0 = 1$**\n\n**Formula:** $x_{n+1} = x_n - \\frac{f(x_n)}{f'(x_n)}$ where $f'(x) = 3x^2$\n\n**Iteration 1:** $x_0 = 1$\n$$f(1) = 1 - 2 = -1, \\quad f'(1) = 3$$\n$$x_1 = 1 - \\frac{-1}{3} = 1 + \\frac{1}{3} = \\frac{4}{3} \\approx 1.333$$\n\n**Iteration 2:** $x_1 = \\frac{4}{3}$\n$$f\\left(\\frac{4}{3}\\right) = \\left(\\frac{4}{3}\\right)^3 - 2 = \\frac{64}{27} - 2 = \\frac{10}{27}$$\n$$f'\\left(\\frac{4}{3}\\right) = 3\\left(\\frac{4}{3}\\right)^2 = \\frac{16}{3}$$\n$$x_2 = \\frac{4}{3} - \\frac{10/27}{16/3} = \\frac{4}{3} - \\frac{10}{27} \\cdot \\frac{3}{16} = \\frac{4}{3} - \\frac{5}{72} = \\frac{96-5}{72} = \\frac{91}{72} \\approx 1.264$$\n\n**Result:** After 2 iterations, $x_2 \\approx 1.264$ (actual $\\sqrt[3]{2} \\approx 1.2599$)",
